# Wiki Index Template

Content-oriented catalog. This is the master index of everything in the wiki. Each page is listed with a link, one-line summary, and metadata like date or source count. Organized by category (sources, entities, concepts, synthesis). The LLM updates this on every ingest. When answering queries, the LLM reads index.md first to find relevant pages, then drills into them. This works well at moderate scale (~100 sources, hundreds of pages) and avoids the need for embedding-based RAG.

